{
	"_source": "CPR core p.337-339 (Night Markets, Night Market Generator, On the Shelves), p.340 onward (Night Market Appendix: what each item is and costs; prices come from weapons.json, armor.json, gear.json, cyberware.json). Listing names are the book's row labels; numbers and short paraphrases only.",
	"_doc": "Campaign/NightMarket read this. A listing's 'keys' are storage keys (Items: weapon/<id>, armor/<id>, <section>/<id>, cyberware/<id>); a weapon key stands for every Quality Rating of it (p338). A 'filter' picks every item matching kind (weapon|armor|kit|cyberware), section (kit), category (weapon or cyberware), option (cyberware that needs a foundation), cost / cost_max / cost_min (list eb); 'choose': n takes n of them at random (the book's 'of GM's choice'). Only what the game plays is ever on sale (weapons/armor/kit marked sold, cyberware the Ripperdoc installs); a listing with neither keys nor filter has no counterpart in the game's data and is shown for flavour.",
	"categories_roll": {
		"dice": "1d6",
		"times": 2,
		"reroll_duplicates": true,
		"cite": "CPR core p.338: roll 1d6 twice for the goods sold; reroll a repeat."
	},
	"listings_roll": {
		"count_dice": "1d10",
		"row_dice": "1d100",
		"reroll_duplicates": true,
		"all_qualities": true,
		"cite": "CPR core p.338: per category, 1d10 types of items; d100 that many times on its column, rerolling a repeat; an item with Quality Ratings is there in all of them; a listing is a type of goods, not the whole inventory."
	},
	"cyberware_foundations": {
		"cite": "CPR core p.338: a Cyberware Option rolled brings any Foundational Cyberware it needs. Cyberware bought here isn't installed at the market; the seller sends you to their Ripperdoc for a free installation.",
		"free_install": true
	},
	"house_rules": {
		"open_days": 3,
		"open_days_doc": "HOUSE-RULE: the book gives no schedule (p337: markets pop up without warning, for a few hours or regularly at a site). One market is up at a time; it stays open 3 days, then the next one is rolled.",
		"quantity_doc": "HOUSE-RULE reading: the book gives no quantities (p338: a listing is a type of goods, not the total inventory), so a listed item can be bought any number of times while the market is up.",
		"access_doc": "No Reputation gate: p337 says finding a market is about connections, with no number; the crew's fixers bring them in."
	},
	"staples": {
		"max_cost": 100,
		"doc": "Owner's ruling, from CPR core p.385: without a Fixer or Night Market, items up to Premium (100eb) can be bought. So every item the game plays at 100eb or less (weapons at Standard quality, armour, kit items) is always on sale; pricier gear only at a Night Market."
	},
